From f8550630dde3c0478002ff6d8e578f203b907d84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allan Siriani <allan@fatecpompeia.edu.br>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:42:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] slimbus: qcom-ngd-ctrl: add a PIO mode for the MSM8226
 NGD

The MSM8226 NGD exchanges messages through the NGD_TX_MSG (0x30) and
NGD_RX_MSG (0x70) registers, as the downstream slim-msm-ngd.c does
until it switches to the BAM queues. The mainline driver only had the
DMA queues, whose BAM pipes are allocated at runtime on this SoC and
are not described in the device tree.

New compatible qcom,slim-ngd-v1.3.0 (or the qcom,pio-mode property):
- TX: write the message word by word to NGD_TX_MSG and wait for
  NGD_INT_TX_MSG_SENT; a NACK or error becomes -EIO (the capability
  worker already retries on -EIO).
- RX: on NGD_INT_RX_MSG_RCVD read NGD_RX_MSG and hand it to the same
  qcom_slim_ngd_rx() used by the DMA path.
- NGD_CFG only gets ENABLE (queues off), no NGD_RX_MSGQ_CFG.
- NGD base from the version read at reg+0 after the QMI vote: version 0
  uses the V1 layout (0x800/0xA00), otherwise V2 (0x1000/0x2000).
  qcom,ngd-offset overrides it.
- No PDR: the MSM8226 ADSP has no service registry. The NGD comes up
  when the SLIMbus QMI service (0x301) appears, and the "lpass" SSR
  still covers ADSP restarts. The up worker does not enable twice.

Changes for both paths: work items and workqueue created before the QMI
lookup, NGD base set before platform_device_add(), flags read before
request_irq().

The DMA path (v1.5.0/v2.1.0) does not change behaviour.

Tested on the Moto G 2013 (falcon): the WCD9306 enumerates and its chip
id reads back 0x0103.

Signed-off-by: Allan Siriani <allan@fatecpompeia.edu.br>
---
